    dict(key='01-poster', kind='poster', title='Keystores and Key Management Basics',
         body=None,
         narration='Hello, and welcome. [[slnc 400]] This video explains keystores and key management, in Java. [[slnc 300]] This video is presented by Jayasekhar Konduru. [[slnc 600]] Key management asks where a key lives, and how it is replaced. [[slnc 300]] A keystore is an encrypted file that holds keys, and opens with a password. [[slnc 600]] Think of a bank with a fortune spent on its vault door, and the key under the doormat. [[slnc 700]] In this video, the domain is an online bank, and its statement key. [[slnc 500]] You will see why each home for a key beats the last. [[slnc 300]] How a key is made from a password, round by round. [[slnc 300]] And how a key is replaced without losing data.'),
